# Changelog on Every Commit

When making any commit that changes user-facing behavior, admin UI, client config, styling, assets, or API behavior, **always update the changelog in the same commit** before pushing.

## Files to update

1. **`CHANGELOG.md`** — add bullets under `## [Unreleased]` in the correct section (`Added`, `Changed`, `Fixed`, `Removed`). Match the existing Keep a Changelog style.
2. **`src/lib/changelog.ts`** — add a new entry at the **top** of the `CHANGELOG` array when the change is worth showing on the Admin → Changelog page. Bump `package.json` version (patch) so the deployed build matches the newest entry.

## Commit workflow

1. Make the code/config change.
2. Update `CHANGELOG.md` (required for every product commit).
3. Update `src/lib/changelog.ts` + `package.json` version when the release should appear in the admin changelog UI.
4. Commit everything together — do **not** leave changelog updates for a follow-up commit.

## What to write

- One bullet per meaningful change; plain English; India/TGA context where relevant.
- No SignalFlow branding in TGA user-facing changelog text unless the change is internal/template-only.

## Skip only when

- Pure tooling/docs with zero product impact (e.g. `.gitignore`, CI-only), or the user explicitly says not to changelog.
